lesson: 194
title: Adding hours and minutes
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: Add the hours to the hours and the minutes to the minutes. If the minutes reach 60 or more, 60 of them make one more hour.
explain: 1 h 45 min + 2 h 30 min = 3 h 75 min = 4 h 15 min, which is 4 × 60 + 15 = 255 minutes.
explain: A time written only in minutes can be added straight to the other time turned into minutes.
vars: a=name h1=1..3 h2=1..3 u=4..11 v=4..11 s=7..10
let: m1 = 5 * u
let: m2 = 5 * v
need: m1 + m2 >= 60
answer: 60 * (h1 + h2) + m1 + m2
exercise: {a} practises the piano for {h1} h {m1} min on Saturday and {h2} h {m2} min on Sunday. How many minutes does {a.he} practise in all?
exercise: A train goes from the first town to the second in {h1} h {m1} min and then on to the third town in {h2} h {m2} min. How many minutes does the whole trip take?
exercise: {a} spends {h1} h {m1} min on homework and {h2} h {m2} min playing outside. How many minutes is that altogether?
exercise: One film lasts {h1} h {m1} min and another lasts {h2} h {m2} min. How many minutes do the two films last together?
exercise: A hike takes {h1} h {m1} min going up the hill and {h2} h {m2} min coming down. How many minutes does the hike take?
test: {a} rode a bus for {60 * h1 + m1} minutes and then a train for {h2} h {m2} min. How many minutes did the ride take altogether?
test: The second part of a journey was {h2} h {m2} min long, and the first part {h1} h {m1} min. Give the length of the whole journey in minutes.
test: How many minutes pass from the start of the first lesson to the end of the second if the first lasts {h1} h {m1} min, the second {h2} h {m2} min, and there is no break between them?
test: {a} left home at {s} o'clock. {a.He} cycled for {h1} h {m1} min and then walked for {h2} h {m2} min. How many minutes was {a.he} on the move?
exercise: {a} reads for {h1} h {m1} min on Monday and {h2} h {m2} min on Tuesday. How many minutes does {a.he} read in total?
exercise: How many minutes does a car trip in two parts take, if the first part takes {h1} h {m1} min and the second {h2} h {m2} min?
exercise: A drive from Leeds to York takes {h1} h {m1} min, and from York on to Durham it takes {h2} h {m2} min. How many minutes does the whole drive take?
exercise: Add {h1} h {m1} min and {h2} h {m2} min. How many minutes is that?
exercise: {a} spends {h1} h {m1} min at the beach and then {h2} h {m2} min at the park. How many minutes is that combined?
exercise: A football tournament in Ontario has a morning session of {h1} h {m1} min and an afternoon session of {h2} h {m2} min. How many minutes of football are played altogether?
exercise: {a} helps on a farm in Queensland for {h1} h and {m1.words} minutes on Saturday and for {h2} h and {m2.words} minutes on Sunday. How many minutes does {a.he} help in all?
exercise: A boat trip in New Zealand has two legs: {h1} h {m1} min out to the island and {h2} h {m2} min back. How many minutes does the trip last?
test: How long, in minutes, are two plays together, if the first runs for {h1} h {m1} min and the second for {h2} h {m2} min?
test: On a long flight to Sydney, {a} sleeps for {h1} h {m1} min, wakes up, and then sleeps again for {h2} h {m2} min. For how many minutes does {a.he} sleep altogether?
test: Two TV shows are recorded: one is {h2} h {m2} min long, the other {h1} h {m1} min. How many minutes of recording is that?
test: A bike race in Wales has a first stage of {h1} h {m1} min and a second stage of {h2} h {m2} min for the winner. What is the winner's total time in minutes?
test: Starting at {s} o'clock, {a} paints a fence for {h1} h {m1} min and then mows the lawn for {h2} h {m2} min. How many minutes does {a.he} work?
test: In minutes, how long does {a} spend on a train journey across Canada that has two parts, lasting {h1} h {m1} min and {h2} h {m2} min?
exercise: {a} did piano {h1} h {m1} min sat and {h2} h {m2} min sun, how many mins all up
exercise: train {h1} h {m1} min to first stop then {h2} h {m2+5} — no wait, {h2} h {m2} min. whole trip in mins?
exercise: watched a movie {h1} h {m1} min then another one {h2} h {m2} min, ate 2 bags popcorn lol. how many mins we watched
exercise: {a} says {h1} h {m1} min plus {h2} h {m2} min is {h1+h2+m1+m2} minutes lol. nah. how many minutes really
test: bus {60*h1+m1} mins then train {h2} h {m2} min, total mins?
test: hiked {h1} h {m1} min up, {h2} h {m2} min down, took 3 water bottles. mins altogether?
test: {a} reckons {h1} h {m1} n {h2} h {m2} is like {100*(h1+h2)+m1+m2} mins?? whats the real number of minutes
exam: It is given that {a} practises the piano for {h1} hours {m1} minutes on Saturday and for {h2} hours {m2} minutes on Sunday. Determine the aggregate duration of practice, expressed in minutes.
exam: A railway journey consists of two stages, of durations {h1} h {m1} min and {h2} h {m2} min respectively. Ascertain the total duration of the journey in minutes.
exam: Whereas two periods of time measure {h1} hours and {m1} minutes and {h2} hours and {m2} minutes, state their sum expressed solely in minutes.
exam: Compute, in minutes, the combined duration of two films, the first being of {h1} hours {m1} minutes and the second of {h2} hours {m2} minutes in length.
exercise: {a}'s dad was furloughed, so instead of his usual 8-hour shift he did {h1} h {m1} min of jobs at home on Monday and {h2} h {m2} min on Tuesday. How many minutes did he work at home in all?
exercise: Grandma went under the knife for her hip: the 'procedure' took {h1} h {m1} min, and then she was in recovery for {h2} h {m2} min. How many minutes was that altogether?
test: bloody train had a 'technical hiccup' so the trip took {h1} h {m1} min, then the bus {h2} h {m2} min. how many minutes total, i'm knackered
